SYSTEMCTL - control the CloverOS init system
Usage: systemctl <action> [unit]

Manages session units: dependencies, targets, enable/disable state and
the default boot target, over the kernel service table.

list-units      (default) table of every unit and its state
status [unit]   detail for one unit, or the default target
start <unit>    start a unit and everything it depends on
stop <unit>     stop a unit
restart <unit>  stop then start a unit
enable <unit>   start the unit at session boot
disable <unit>  leave the unit out of the boot
is-active <u>   print active/inactive
is-enabled <u>  print enabled/disabled
set-default <target>  change the boot target

Units: network, cloverd, sshd, multi-user.target, graphical.target.
Enabled units start with the session; wants fail without failing their
target. Enable state persists in /etc/clover/init.cfg.

Examples:
  systemctl start sshd
  systemctl disable cloverd
  systemctl set-default graphical.target
